added. this would be okay if i were grabbing multiple leads from one sheet, but each photo i import represents only one lead...not multiple. i think we need to abandon the whole 'list' philosophy and just recognize that we're working with a bunch of individual leads. we can capture the date/time the entered the system, but maintaining entire separate lists with dates is not necessary\"`, `\"deploy it to surge please...and do so going forward after every new compile\"`\n  - *Status:* **IMPLEMENTATION** (Files `ListsScreen.tsx`, `ScanSheetScreen.tsx`, and `leadsRepository.ts` updated; need to verify build export `npx expo export -p web`, inject PWA tags into `dist/index.html`, and execute `npx surge ./dist valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh`).\n\n---\n\n## 2. User Knowledge\n- **Domain & Workflow Rules:**\n  - Target Company: **ValuTeachers** working with Florida educators on the **Florida Retirement System (FRS)** and **403(b)/457(b)** plans.\n  - Call Goal: **45-minute planning period in-person classroom sit-down**.\n  - **Single Lead Workflow:** Each photo snapped represents **ONE educator lead**, not a multi-lead roster. The user explicitly directed: *\"abandon the whole 'list' philosophy and just recognize that we're working with a bunch of individual leads.\"*\n  - **Model Version Requirement:** The user explicitly reported: `\"i'm getting an error that gemini-2.5-flash is no longer available to new users and to update the code to use gemini-3.6-flash\"`.\n  - **Auto-Deploy Rule:** The user explicitly commanded: `\"deploy it to surge please...and do so going forward after every new compile\"`.\n  - Live Surge Domain: **`https://valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh`**.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Work Accomplished\n1. **Model Endpoint Upgrade to Gemini 3.6 Flash:**\n   - Updated `VisionService.ts` and `AiSmsService.ts` to use `gemini-3.6-flash` as primary with automatic fallback across `['gemini-3.6-flash', 'gemini-2.0-flash', 'gemini-1.5-flash']`.\n2. **Fixed Settings Sync & Caller Name Injection:**\n   - `AiSmsService` dynamically pulls `user_name` from local SQLite/storage and injects it into both Gemini prompts and fallback templates.\n   - `SettingsScreen.tsx` adds instant save confirmation banner.\n3. **Cross-Platform Delete & SQL Fixes:**\n   - Added SQL handlers in `WebDatabase` (`database.ts`) for `DELETE FROM leads WHERE id = ?`.\n   - Replaced browser-incompatible `Alert.alert` buttons with cross-platform confirmation dialogs (`window.confirm` on web/mobile Safari).\n4. **Shifted from \"Lists\" to Master Individual Lead Pipeline:**\n   - Updated `leadsRepository.ts` with `addSingleLead()`, `getAllLeads()`, `getMasterDialingQueue()`, `deleteLead()`, and `recycleUnansweredLeads()`.\n   - Redesigned `ListsScreen.tsx` into a unified **Educator Lead Hub / Pipeline** with search, filter tabs (*All*, *To Call*, *Sit-Downs*, *Callbacks*, *Unanswered*), KPI stats strip, and 1-tap **\"▶ Start Power Dialing Queue\"** CTA.\n   - Redesigned `ScanSheetScreen.tsx` for single report card capture with instant verification and direct \"Save Educator to Pipeline\" / \"Save & Open Call HUD\".\n\n---\n\n## 4. Model Knowledge\n- **WebDatabase Storage Layer (`src/db/database.ts`):**\n  - Manages relational SQLite state via browser localStorage for PWA mode.\n  - Queries for `from leads` support master queue filtering across all dispositions without requiring `list_id`.\n- **Surge Deploy Pipeline:**\n  - Build command: `npx expo export -p web`\n  - Re-inject iOS standalone meta tags (`apple-mobile-web-app-capable`) and `dist/manifest.json`.\n  - Deploy command: `npx surge ./dist valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Files and Code\n\n### Edited Files\n- `src/db/leadsRepository.ts`: Added `addSingleLead`, `getAllLeads`, `getMasterDialingQueue`, `deleteLead`, and `recycleUnansweredLeads`.\n- `src/screens/ListsScreen.tsx`: Complete overhaul from nested lists to a flat, searchable, filterable individual educator lead dashboard with 1-tap dial queue.\n- `src/screens/ScanSheetScreen.tsx`: Streamlined single card verification UI; removed list title inputs; added 1-tap single lead save/dial.\n- `src/services/visionService.ts`: Upgraded to `gemini-3.6-flash`, fixed base64 web ingestion, eliminated silent fallback to demo data.\n- `src/services/aiSmsService.ts`: Upgraded to `gemini-3.6-flash`, dynamic caller name from settings.\n- `src/db/database.ts`: Added `DELETE FROM leads` and general update handlers to `WebDatabase.runAsync`.\n- `src/screens/SettingsScreen.tsx`: Added auto-save feedback banner and dynamic caller name persistence.\n- `dist/index.html` & `dist/manifest.json`: Injected iOS standalone PWA headers.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n1. Run `npx expo export -p web` in `C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\snap-dialer`.\n2. Ensure `dist/index.html` has the iOS PWA meta tags and `dist/manifest.json` is written.\n3. Deploy to Surge: `npx surge ./dist valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh`.\n4. Prompt the user to refresh their iPhone app to test the new flat individual lead workflow with Gemini 3.6 Flash.\n\nYou have the 4 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1787239731075]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/brain/9c9b5ef4-82a1-483f-9e9e-cb421c9396b3/.user_uploaded/media_1787239731075.jpg\nLast Edited: 2026-08-20T15:30:15Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1787239731084]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/brain/9c9b5ef4-82a1-483f-9e9e-cb421c9396b3/.user_uploaded/media_1787239731084.jpg\nLast Edited: 2026-08-20T15:30:15Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: implementation_plan]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/brain/9c9b5ef4-82a1-483f-9e9e-cb421c9396b3/implementation_plan.md\nLast Edited: 2026-08-20T15:30:28Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: walkthrough]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/brain/9c9b5ef4-82a1-483f-9e9e-cb421c9396b3/walkthrough.md\nLast Edited: 2026-08-20T17:59:20Z\n\n# Conversation Logs\n\nReference the following log files for the full, un